{"segs": ["PA_thig_1.2:0.1", "PA_thig_1.2:0.2"], "en": "Therīgāthā 1.2 Ekakanipāta:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thig_1.2:0.3"], "en": "The Verses of the Nun Muttā", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thig_1.2:1.1"], "en": "“O Muttā, may you be released from the bonds,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thig_1.2:1.2"], "en": "like the moon from the grasp of Rāhu;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thig_1.2:1.3"], "en": "with a mind completely liberated, [may you attain peace].”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thig_1.2:1.4"], "en": "\"Eat your almsfood free from debt.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_thig_1.2:2.1"], "en": "In this way, it is said, the Blessed One frequently exhorted the trainee Mutta with this verse.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T13:03:48Z"}
